---
title: Quickstart
description: Create a portal, preview it, and build it for production.
---

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 22.12 or later
- One or more OpenAPI 3.0, 3.1 or Swagger 2.0 files (optional: the starter includes one)

## Create a portal

{% steps %}
{% step title="Scaffold the project" %}
```bash
npm create rapidoc@latest my-portal
```

In a repository that already has OpenAPI files, run `npx rapidoc init` there instead. It finds the specs and asks which to list under `apis:`, the site title, and whether to install the dependencies, then prints the command that does the same without questions. Options: `--title "Acme Developers"`, `--spec <file>` (repeatable), `--no-install`, `--force` to overwrite existing files, and `--yes` to take the defaults without asking.
{% /step %}

{% step title="Start the dev server" %}
```bash
cd my-portal
npm run dev
```

The portal opens on `http://localhost:4321`. Guide edits appear immediately; a change to `rapidoc.config.yaml` or a spec restarts the server.
{% /step %}

{% step title="Make it yours" %}
Edit `rapidoc.config.yaml`: the site title and logo, the theme color, the header tabs and the sidebar. Write guides in `docs/`. See [Configuration](/docs/configuration/overview/) and [Writing guides](/docs/writing/markdown/).
{% /step %}

{% step title="Build for production" %}
```bash
npm run build
```

The static site is written to `dist/`. Upload it to any static host: see [Static hosting](/docs/deploy/static-hosting/).
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

## What the starter contains

```text
my-portal/
├── rapidoc.config.yaml   # site, header, tabs, theme, APIs
├── package.json          # dev, build and validate scripts
├── specs/api.yaml        # a starter spec (or your own specs)
├── docs/
│   ├── index.markdoc     # the home page
│   ├── getting-started.md
│   └── guides/overview.markdoc
└── .gitignore            # node_modules/, dist/, .rapidoc-temp/
```

Read on in [Project structure](/docs/getting-started/project-structure/).

## Check your specs in CI

```bash
npx rapidoc validate
```

It checks every local spec in `apis:` against the OpenAPI schema and exits with code 1 on an error. See [Validate](/docs/tools/validate/).

## Keep it private

To put the portal, or some of its pages and APIs, behind your company's single sign-on (Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, Google, Keycloak), see [Single sign-on (SSO) and access](/docs/access/overview/).
